<metadata>
  <!--
    io.agora.board.fast.ui is Fastboard's own toolbar implementation — the button, layout and
    RecyclerView.Adapter subclasses it assembles the control bar from. class-parse cannot generate
    most of it: the adapters subclass RecyclerView.Adapter<VH> and lose the type argument to
    erasure, so the generated classes never satisfy the abstract onBindViewHolder (CS0534), and the
    layouts implement FastVisiable with covariant returns the generator cannot express (CS0535).

    The whole package is removed rather than patched class by class. Nothing outside Fastboard
    constructs these: an app adds a FastboardView, and the toolbar assembles itself. The one type
    in there a consumer *does* touch is FastUiSettings, which configures the toolbar — it stays,
    along with the enums and the drawable, because none of them has the problem.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ApplianceAdapter']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ColorAdapter']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ToolboxAdapter']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ErrorHandleLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ExtensionButton']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ExtensionLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='FastRoomController']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='LoadingLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='OverlayLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='RedoUndoLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='RoomControllerGroup']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ScenesLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ToolButton']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ToolLayout']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.ui']/class[@name='ToolboxLayout']" />

  <!--
    The replay surface — playback of a recorded session — is not bound.

    Two reasons, and the second is the one that decides it.

    It cannot stay as it is: FastReplayListener and FastRoomListener both declare onFastError and
    both live in io.agora.board.fast, so the generator emits a FastErrorEventArgs partial for each
    and the two merge into a single class carrying both sets of fields (CS0102). A rename would
    fix that much — the Chat binding does exactly that for its chat-room listener.

    But it should not stay at all: replay is playback of a recorded session, a separate feature
    from drawing on a live board. Net.Agora.Fastboard does not expose it, and neither does this
    repository's iOS counterpart — the shim in sbokatuk/Net.Agora.iOS's native/AgoraFastboardBridge
    — so binding it on one platform only would be an asymmetry with nothing behind it. Renaming to
    keep a surface no façade reaches would be the worse trade.

    The classes stay in the .aar; what is removed is the managed view of them. Re-attempt this the
    day replay is worth exposing, on both platforms.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast']/interface[@name='FastReplayListener']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast']/interface[@name='OnReplayReadyCallback']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast']/class[@name='FastReplay']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.internal']/class[@name='FastReplayContext']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='io.agora.board.fast.model']/class[@name='FastReplayOptions']" />
</metadata>
